{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-28","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：整数","englishTitle":"If an odd number by multiplying an even number make some number, the product will be even.","book":9,"number":28,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":28,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","contentId":"euclid-9-28","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a1a588d152dcd410eedbe046a10cf0247d26e774582af457eba2f6509acf3f5a","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-28.statement","euclid-9-28.construction.1","euclid-9-28.proof.1","euclid-9-28.proof.2","euclid-9-28.proof.3","euclid-9-28.conclusion","euclid-9-28.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-28.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5cde1e91e46449d36d6ca2d7c383eb12c7c5a079bf9257d02b98891a03c79ab8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If an odd number by multiplying an even number make some number, the product will be even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果一个奇数乘以一个偶数,得出了某个数字,则产品是偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9a13774b4c010edc0fd10cedc76696b7097f3f0518a8ea960432d774b4c3887b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the odd number A by multiplying the even number B make C; I say that C is even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"将B偶数乘以A偶数,就等于C偶数;我说C偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"44f71ed68b5793e57155ca8eb29f991fdc4aabd5ee114bda61b2bde4fd620e23","citations":["euclid-7-def-15"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since A by multiplying B has made C, therefore C is made up of as many numbers equal to B as there are units in A. [[VII. Def. 15](/principles/euclid-7-def-15)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,A乘以B, 已经组成C, 因此C由B和A的单位组成。 [[VII. Def. 15](/principles/euclid-7-def-15)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"68451af3130ef47ea55948277103abd042b72919d73aa9be7476ea2de9984f23","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And B is even; therefore C is made up of even numbers."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"B是平的,因此C是平的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d271a06a9b647a3f60038d6656cc9673e86633fba9e5ca3c37011f7e92d5b08","citations":["euclid-9-21"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, if as many even numbers as we please be added together, the whole is even. [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,如果我们想加多少数字,就加多少,整个数字是公平的。 [[IX. 21](/principles/euclid-9-21)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":5,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bc6e57edb36228e92debf291a5b755b406d23755cc0aa556702faff2fc730585","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore C is even. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,C是平的,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-28.source","contentId":"euclid-9-28","revisionId":"euclid-9-28@raw-a1a588d152dcd410","order":6,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"361ffe85885b57bb507da3cc5907090f5ed04bb29a1574e96f0e1b71aacea0ef","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-9-28:euclid-7-def-15:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-28","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-28.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-def-15","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28/","sourceLabel":"VII. Def. 15"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-9-28:euclid-9-21:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-28","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-28.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-9-21","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.28/","sourceLabel":"IX. 21"}}],"incomingEdges":[],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-9-28:euclid-7-def-15:explicit","id":"euclid-7-def-15","book":7,"number":15,"kind":"definition","title":"整数乘法：重复相加","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"},{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-9-28:euclid-9-21:explicit","id":"euclid-9-21","book":9,"number":21,"kind":"proposition","title":"偶数之和仍为偶数","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-number","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
